commit 4318fbde616f6347e232541b308e7f6dbffbebff
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Wed Jul 29 16:31:09 2026 -0400

    Bring small file bundling over to serial sftp/scp transfers.
    
      When using workers, even a single worker via -j1, small files are
      bundled and transferred using a tar like process that reduces
      the per file overhead in serial transfers. This brings that bundle
      concept over to serial transfers. That let's us avoid the use of
      spawning a secondary worker (as with -j1) and is more in line
      with user expectations. This is *largely* the same mechanics as
      bundling in -j mode but it is currently missing the pipeline
      used to start assembling and moving bundles before the final
      acknowledgement for the previous bundle. That's a slight
      performance hit that will be addressed in the next commit.

commit b4b59a7ae6f209b20a9caaa86c0899b02c8a91b4
