commit 34efbe67d9fed8cf2b9553b157a75f4372fe3432
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Tue Jul 28 18:42:02 2026 -0400

    Remove the output-buffer grant taper from channel_check_window.
    
      Instrumented famine runs never engaged the taper code. Its band
      is unreachable: c->output occupancy is fed only by granted credit and
      credit is granted only against consumption, so occupancy cannot exceed
      one window. The taper also silently discarded the un-granted portion
      of local_consumed on any partial grant, which would have permanently
      shrunk the effective window had the band ever been reached. Grants
      return to stock behaviour plus the dynamic-window addition; memory
      remains bounded by the window itself, which HPNMemoryLimit clamps.

