commit 0139a0d82795c210ce49303bd4c699ee977ee0ae
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Wed Jul 15 16:55:19 2026 -0400

    Scale the SSH channel window by the decompression ratio.
    
      Transport compression collapsed single-stream throughput on high-BDP
      paths: a 10gbit/75ms transfer of compressible data capped near 99 MiB/s
      regardless of compression ratio, far below the ~280 MiB/s of an
      uncompressed stream.
    
      The cause is a units mismatch in channel_tcpwinsz. The channel window is
      derived from the receiver's rcv_space, a wire-level (post-compression)
      BDP estimate, but it flow-controls plaintext channel data. When
      compression shrinks the wire bytes, rcv_space -- and therefore the
      window -- is sized several times too small for the plaintext data rate,
      so both compressed flows bottom out at the 8 MiB CHANNEL_OUTPUT_HWM_FLOOR
      (the ratio-independent ~99 MiB/s cap).
    
      Track the incoming decompression expansion ratio in hpn_zstd_in and
      multiply rcv_space by it in channel_tcpwinsz, converting the wire BDP
      into a plaintext BDP before the window is derived. The window's own
      rcv_space feedback then ramps it up to fill the path.

commit ea5145dc74adf2bb29107ef94ada93fe5fb40cbc
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Tue Jul 14 11:03:38 2026 -0400

    Fail soft on zero-length SFTP reads; fix fleet-abort escape and exit status.
    
      Convert upstream's zero-length-read guard from fatal_f to the sftp_conn_die
      in sftp_download and sftp_crossload. A broken or malicious server answering
      reads with empty DATA could kill the whole parallel orchestrator from a
      worker thread. Serial transfers now fail once, legibly.
      Parallel workers fail soft and respawn untile a threshhold is met that
      brings down the entrie process. This is to prevent an endless loop.
    
      Note: The fleet abort could never fire. the no-progress counter borrowed
      the sync-stall window position as its first-tick guard, so the
      window wrap zeroed it every 20 ticks, capping it below any legal
      HPNStallAbortTimeout. Give it a dedicated first-sample flag.
    
      An aborted transfer exited 0: a fleet abort abandons pending units
      without recording per-unit failures, so parallel_flush's aggregates
      missed it. Refuse success via sftp_parallel_was_aborted and report
      the unfinished unit count.
    
      Dead-connection read failures printed a "No error" status. This
      was confusing and pointless. Omit the status clause when no
      status code was ever received.
    
      Also demote the BUNDLE-DL per-bundle stats line from logit to debug,
      matching the upload side.

commit f798e94a141022ba4f7934aef7aa302a79f2940f
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
