commit 2660f7ca1a21ab157bf7fc7589388beda5e90c08
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Sat Jul 11 22:20:10 2026 -0400

    Never kill throughput outliers; mark them stalled instead
    
      Slower-than-sibling is not evidence of death: on a saturated path TCP
      fairness starves some streams while their peers run at line rate, and
      a respawn inherits the same contention.  The outlier classifier was
      SIGTERMing such workers with silence=0s - actively transferring - and
      took down a single-file range-split transfer with them (2026-07-09).
    
      The tput-outlier path now only marks the worker STALLED for telemetry;
      the DEAD promotion, its doom reason, and the one-kill-per-tick
      throttle are gone.  Genuinely degraded sessions are still reaped by
      born-slow (absolute floor, healthy-peer and cooldown gated) and the
      silence paths.  Man page and classifier docs updated to match.

