commit 3abfd4dbba3a0d82c315bde40d281950713d60e3
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Thu Jul 9 12:43:00 2026 -0400

    hpn3scp: relay FILEFAIL frames to the front-end as EVENT file_fail
    
      Wire the FILEFAIL frame through the launcher: a run hook (on_file_fail)
      off the parser, and an hpn3scp handler that percent-encodes the opaque
      path and emits "EVENT file_fail kind=N path=<pct>", tallying verify vs
      transfer failures for the upcoming completion summary. Human mode stays
      silent - the source's stderr already carries the per-file detail.
    
      Add pct_encode_n (length-delimited) so a path with embedded NULs or
      non-NUL-terminated bytes encodes fully; pct_encode becomes a strlen
      wrapper. The borrowed frame path is consumed in the callback, not kept.

