commit abfa0b52c6aec5684c6a7165d5dc623a3ce4de45
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Wed Jul 8 18:28:47 2026 -0400

    Fuzzers for the Add fuzz harness for the hpn3scp keyscan-line parser
    
      The launcher has the (possibly hostile) source keyscan the target,
      and every returned byte reaches this parser. The harness feeds arbitrary
      input line-by-line, mirroring the real consumer's strtok_r split,
      and asserts the parser's contract - an accepted line always yields a key,
      a skip/reject never leaks one, and markers and malformed keys
      are always rejected.
    
      The seed-corpus generator covers valid keys in several hostspec forms,
      the reject cases (@cert-authority/@revoked markers, garbage, truncated
      base64), and the skip cases (comments, blanks).

commit 70edea383b80c47abc4966f71f2b95441dbc35c7
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Wed Jul 8 16:14:46 2026 -0400

    hpn3scp Stage 3: source-key-only auth, preflight, tty front-end
    
      Default is now SOURCE-KEY-ONLY: the source authenticates to the target
      with its own key, so the user's key never leaves the launch host and no
      agent is ever forwarded. -A opts into forwarding the ambient agent for
      sources with no key on the target, gated by precondition checks (agent
      present, non-empty).
    
      An A->C auth preflight runs before any worker spawns; failures are
      classified (auth / host key / unreachable) and reported with the real
      hostnames and a copy-pasteable fix (ssh-copy-id on the source, or -A).
    
      A managed destination-constrained agent was investigated and rejected:
      ssh-agent refuses to sign on a forwarding hop by design, which is
      exactly what a third-party transfer would need.
    
      Output now has two renderings picked by isatty(stdout): a terminal gets
      plain-text errors on stderr and a local progress meter driven from the
      status frames; a pipe gets the EVENT protocol unchanged.

