commit cdca5b27d0f3a56fdd7e65dfeda99e1023ffe65a
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Tue Jul 7 21:13:47 2026 -0400

    hpn3scp: working transfer, verbosity, option pass-through
    
      Turn the hpn3scp skeleton into a working third-party launcher
      and add pass-through of options to the source hpnscp.
    
      Real endpoint parsing (scp:// URI or [user@]host:path); user validated
      as scp's okname does; local paths rejected (needs two remote hosts).
    
      Source-binary discovery: probe with `command -v hpnscp` and invoke by
      absolute path (HPN3SCP_REMOTE_HPNSCP overrides), so PATH shadowing on
      the source fails early and legibly instead of mid-transfer.
    
      Launch + monitor: build the ssh -> source hpnscp command (env-armed
      frames, -j / -P injected) and relay its status frames as events through
      the shared runner; raw remote bytes are discarded, never on the
      protocol stdout.
    
      Add hpn_run_capture() to the runner for short one-shot probes.
    
      -v now propagates to the launch ssh and the source hpnscp, and hpn3scp
      logs the discovered path and assembled command under -v.
      Also pass through -r (recursive), -o (ssh options -> hpnscp -o),
      -X (sftp options -> hpnscp -X), and -Y (a quoted string of native
      hpnscp switches, split with quote/escape handling).
      hpn3scp stays ignorant of hpnscp's flag set, so new flags just work.

