commit 0caadbbb2f5bc309385791473e33d77916feff40
Author: Chris Rapier <rapier@psc.edu>
Date:   Tue Jul 7 13:06:55 2026 -0400

    Add a live progress meter for scp -R (third party) transfers
    
      A transfer client whose stdout is a pipe emits small numbers-only
      binary status frames (new hpn-status-frame.h) from the existing 1 Hz
      progressmeter tick when armed via HPN_ENABLE_REMOTE_PROGRESS; the
      launching hpnscp injects that variable as an "env" command prefix,
      pipes the launch ssh's stdout, parses the frames, and renders a local
      meter.  An env prefix rather than a flag so old or stock sources
      ignore the request instead of failing; a peer that never speaks
      frames degrades silently to today's behavior.  Frame parse errors
      fall back to verbatim passthrough - the status stream is telemetry,
      never control.  The scp->hpnscp command rewrite learns to skip the
      env prefix.  The parallel reporter feeds worker health counts into
      the frames.  Covers serial and parallel transfers both; fuzz harness
      for the frame parser included.

